I chose these values to keep the cart‑position weight near zero (no direct bias), while giving strong opposing gains on the two link angles (sin θ₁ ≈ 4.5, sin θ₂ ≈ ‑4.5) and their cosines (0.5 and –0.5) so the controller pushes back toward vertical. The negative weights on cart velocity (‑2.0) and both angular velocities (‑3.0) provide aggressive damping of drift and swing, reducing action saturation and preventing the large bias observed in earlier runs. Setting the bias term to zero avoids systematic drift, aiming for a near‑zero control output at the upright equilibrium and thus a much longer, stable episode.
